diff --git a/docs/data-transfers.md b/docs/data-transfers.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0cd2156
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/data-transfers.md
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# Moving data into and out of Fizzy
+
+Administrators can request a full account export in **Account Settings**. Every
+member can request an export of their visible cards from their own
+profile. Both run in background jobs. The requester receives an email containing
+a private download link, valid for 24 hours from completion. Treat the link and
+ZIP as sensitive account data. Expired exports are cleaned up hourly.
+
+Sign in, then visit `/account/imports/new` (without an account-number prefix) to
+upload a full account ZIP. Imports create a new account; they never merge into or
+overwrite an existing account. The importing identity becomes an owner and can
+access all restored boards. Other people are matched by email address; existing
+identities, credentials, and accounts are not modified. Deactivated people remain
+deactivated. A completion email links to the new account. Failures send an
+explanation, roll back the restored data, and remove newly uploaded files. Source
+uploads are removed after processing, whether the import succeeds or fails.
+
+## ZIP format, version 1
+
+- `manifest.json`: format version, export kind (`account` or `cards`), and account
+  information. Only full `account` exports can be imported.
+- `cards/<id>.json`: a card's attributes, portable HTML description, comments with
+  their HTML bodies, and attachment metadata with paths to the actual files.
+- `files/<blob-id>`: the original attachment bytes. Original filenames and media
+  types are recorded in `blobs.jsonl` and the card JSON.
+- `attachments.jsonl`, `blobs.jsonl`: attachment associations and file metadata.
+- `records/<table>.jsonl`: full account exports also contain restore records for
+  people, board access and publication, columns, cards, comments, tags, steps,
+  assignments, closures, watches, pins, reactions, mentions, activity, notification
+  history, saved filters, retention settings, user preferences, and rich text.
+
+Public board keys, record IDs, attachment keys, and rich-text signed IDs are
+regenerated on import. Storage accounting and search indexes are rebuilt.
+Authentication secrets, API tokens, login sessions, push subscriptions, outgoing
+webhooks, notification delivery queues, derived image variants, and prior
+imports/exports are intentionally not transferred. Importing will not replay
+historical events, send invitations, or fire webhooks.
+
+## Operations
+
+Run database migrations and ensure the job workers and email delivery are
+configured. Disk and S3 storage are supported. ZIP64 output streams files in
+chunks (including S3 multipart output); imports read storage ranges rather than
+downloading the entire ZIP. Memory usage is proportional to record/entry metadata,
+not attachment bytes. Temporary disk space must accommodate a disk-backed export
+or the largest individual file being imported. The web server/proxy's upload size
+and timeout settings must permit the account ZIP being uploaded.
+
+The importer validates ZIP entry sizes and CRCs, attachment checksums, record IDs,
+and references. It never extracts archive-provided paths into the filesystem or
+constantizes model names from an upload. JSON records are limited to 64 MiB each;
+attachment files are not subject to that limit.
